A recursive component handing bare children to its own recursion, on the
three targets that build it from a copy.

`frame` is a cycle member, so it is built at run time, and every site that
hands it children gets a copy with them spliced in
(runtime_instance_bare_children.txtar). The copy's body is `frame`'s, so it
holds the recursive site again, and copying that one in turn would never
stop. passInstanceSlots keys a copy by the template site it was made for and
by where that site's children were cloned from: the window's site gets
`frame__slot0`, the recursive site inside it gets `frame__slot2`, and the
recursive site inside `frame__slot2` is the same template site with children
cloned from the same `level {n}`, so it instantiates `frame__slot2` itself.
The site alone is not enough, since two callers' copies hold clones of one site
with different children (runtime_instance_bare_children_forwarded.txtar,
runtime_instance_bare_children_recursive_forwarded.txtar). What `level {n}`
reads is `n` of the level above, lifted to a prop of the level below.

`frame__slot1` is the copy the declaration's own recursive site was given
before anything knew the declaration was dead. Once both sites that render
`frame` render copies, nothing instantiates `frame` or that copy, and neither
is emitted.

deny out/go/fyne/model.go `type Frame(__slot1)?Instance ` -- every site that renders frame renders a copy, so neither the declaration nor its own site's copy is instantiated; html prunes a factory nothing names on its own
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `type Frame(__slot1)?Instance ` -- as above, for the gtk4 record
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}

component frame(n int, content ...component node) node {
    var open = true

    vbox {
        content
        if n > 0 {
            frame(n=n - 1) {
                text(value="level {n}")
            }
        }
    }
}

var depth = 2

window {
    vbox {
        frame(n=depth) {
            text(value="top")
        }
        button(text="deeper", @click { depth += 1 })
    }
}
